---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
// The study system, for a friend: one message to paste into Claude Code, which clones the public copy of the tutor
// and guides them, one small step at a time, to a first lesson. In English, linked only from the welcome page
// (and /nora), out of search engines.
---

<Base
	title="The study system"
	description="A Socratic tutor for your own courses, in Claude Code: paste one message, and your Claude guides you to your first lesson."
	noindex
	lang="en"
>
	<h1>The study system</h1>
	<p>This tutor teaches you your own courses, one slide at a time, then has you do the exercises, without ever giving you the answer before you try. You find it yourself, so you remember it.</p>
	<p>On your Mac, open the Claude app, go to the Code tab, pick a folder (Documents, for example), and paste this message:</p>
	<div class="prompt">
		<pre><code id="prompt">Clone https://github.com/ulysseGagne/study-system into this folder, then read study-system/CLAUDE.md and follow it. It's my first time: guide me one step at a time.</code></pre>
		<button class="copy" type="button" id="copy">Copy</button>
	</div>
	<p>Your Claude takes it from there, one small step at a time, up to your first lesson. When it asks permission to run a command, you can accept.</p>
	<p><strong>Work in progress:</strong> <a href="/tuteur">the tutor demo</a>, in French, shows what a session looks like.</p>

	<script is:inline>
		const button = document.getElementById('copy');
		button.addEventListener('click', async () => {
			const text = document.getElementById('prompt').textContent;
			try {
				await navigator.clipboard.writeText(text);
			} catch {
				const range = document.createRange();
				range.selectNodeContents(document.getElementById('prompt'));
				const selection = getSelection();
				selection.removeAllRanges();
				selection.addRange(range);
				document.execCommand('copy');
			}
			button.textContent = 'Copied';
			setTimeout(() => (button.textContent = 'Copy'), 2000);
		});
	</script>
</Base>

<style>
	/* The message to paste, with its copy button */

	.prompt {
		margin: 0 0 1em;
	}

	.prompt pre {
		margin: 0;
		white-space: pre-wrap;
		overflow-wrap: anywhere;
	}

	.copy {
		display: block;
		margin: 8px 0 0 auto;
		padding: 5px 14px;
		border: 1px solid var(--text);
		border-radius: var(--radius);
		background: var(--text);
		color: var(--bg);
		font: inherit;
		font-size: 15px;
		line-height: 1.4;
		cursor: pointer;
	}

	.copy:hover {
		opacity: 0.85;
	}
</style>
